<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; script-src-attr 'none'; style-src 'self'; connect-src 'none'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'">
  <title>S140 — Complete authorized export rehearsal</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
  <script src="model.js" defer=""></script>
  <script src="lesson.js" defer=""></script>
</head>
<body>
  <a href="#exercise" class="skip">Skip to exercise</a>
  <main>
    <p class="banner" id="training-banner">Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result</p>
    <h1>S140 — The export is not finished at “job completed”</h1>
    <p>Submit, process, poll and inspect a complete authorized download across independently changing tiers.</p>
    <p class="boundary"><strong>Fixed fictional teaching DATA ONLY.</strong> Every request, job, poll, export, artifact, identity, state, tier, failure and timing below is fictional. Buttons only transform fixed in-memory records. Nothing is sent, queued, authenticated, fetched, downloaded or saved. No business or user data is accepted.</p>
    <p><strong>Preconditions:</strong> one fixed owner, one foreign identity, a nine-byte oracle, declared shared-state assumptions and explicit independent transitions. Native storage, authorization and migration remain unverified.</p>
    <section id="exercise" aria-labelledby="exercise-heading">
      <h2 id="exercise-heading">1. Choose a bounded rehearsal</h2>
      <form id="setup" novalidate="">
        <div>
          <label for="condition">Fixed condition</label>
          <select id="condition">
            <option value="preserved">Preserved export</option>
            <option value="artifact-lost">Artifact lost on download v2</option>
            <option value="authorization-lost">Owner authorization lost</option>
            <option value="authorization-bypass">Foreign identity allowed</option>
            <option value="bytes-changed">Same-length artifact bytes changed</option>
            <option value="job-lost">Job state lost on processing v2</option>
            <option value="unobserved">Poll and download unobserved</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="requester">Fictional download requester</label>
          <select id="requester">
            <option value="identity-fiction-owner-140">Intended export owner</option>
            <option value="identity-fiction-other-140">Foreign identity (must be denied)</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="budget">Fictional journey budget (ms)</label>
          <input id="budget" type="text" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[1-9][0-9]{0,2}" maxlength="3" required="" value="40" aria-describedby="budget-help">
          <p id="budget-help">Integer digits only, 1–100. Fixed step clocks total 30 ms; these are not browser or Azure latency measurements.</p>
        </div>
        <button type="submit" id="submit-rehearsal" disabled="">1 Submit fictional export</button>
      </form>
      <p id="error" role="alert" aria-live="assertive">Rejected input/action — Attempt limit: eight (8) fictional journeys. Reload for a new rehearsal.</p>
      <h2>2. Operate each independent transition</h2>
      <div class="actions" aria-label="Ordered fictional operator actions">
        <button type="button" id="switch-process" data-action="switchProcess" disabled="">2 Switch processing to v2</button>
        <button type="button" id="process-job" data-action="process" disabled="">3 Process fictional job</button>
        <button type="button" id="switch-poll" data-action="switchPoll" disabled="">4 Switch polling to v2</button>
        <button type="button" id="poll-job" data-action="poll" disabled="">5 Poll fictional job</button>
        <button type="button" id="switch-download" data-action="switchDownload" disabled="">6 Switch download to v2</button>
        <button type="button" id="inspect-download" data-action="download" disabled="">7 Inspect fictional download bytes</button>
      </div>
      <div class="actions">
        <button type="button" id="check-journey" data-action="check">Check complete authorized journey</button>
        <button type="button" id="reset-active" data-action="reset">Reset active exercise; retain history</button>
      </div>
      <p id="stage">Active stage: ready. Attempt 8 of 8.</p>
      <p id="tiers">Fictional tiers — submit: submit-v1; process: processor-v1; poll: poller-v1; download: download-v1.</p>
      <p>Check early to see what is still unknown. A synthetic HTTP 200 or completed job alone never certifies the complete authorized download journey.</p>
      <p>Limits: eight attempts and 96 retained events per tab. Reset restores default inputs and active state but retains previous checks. Reload starts a new empty rehearsal. There is no persistent storage.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="outcome-heading">
      <h2 id="outcome-heading">3. Measured synthetic client outcome</h2>
      <p id="verdict" class="verdict">UNASSESSED — use Check complete authorized journey.</p>
      <p id="counts">Attempted 8 | Positive 1 | Negative 6 | Unknown 1 | Unassessed 0</p>
      <p id="bytes">Expected fixed bytes: [83,49,52,48,10,49,44,55,10]. No final download bytes observed; do not infer them from a completed job.</p>
      <ol id="checklist"></ol>
      <p>A negative journey can have a correct teaching verifier. Unknown means missing observations, not permission to infer success. No outcome certifies a live Azure result.</p>
      <h3>Retained checks</h3>
      <ol id="results"><li class="unknown">Check 1, attempt 0: UNKNOWN — Unobserved required checks: request, job, poll, artifact, bytes, authorization, isolation, download, transitions, timing.</li><li class="unknown">Check 2, attempt 1: UNKNOWN — Unobserved required checks: artifact, bytes, authorization, isolation, download, transitions, timing.</li><li class="positive">Check 3, attempt 1: POSITIVE — All complete authorized fixed-fiction journey checks passed.</li><li class="negative">Check 4, attempt 2: NEGATIVE — Detected failed client-journey checks: artifact, download.</li><li class="negative">Check 5, attempt 3: NEGATIVE — Detected failed client-journey checks: authorization, download.</li><li class="negative">Check 6, attempt 4: NEGATIVE — Detected failed client-journey checks: isolation.</li><li class="negative">Check 7, attempt 5: NEGATIVE — Detected failed client-journey checks: bytes.</li><li class="negative">Check 8, attempt 6: NEGATIVE — Detected failed client-journey checks: job, poll, artifact, download.</li><li class="unknown">Check 9, attempt 7: UNKNOWN — Unobserved required checks: poll, artifact, bytes, authorization, isolation, download.</li><li class="negative">Check 10, attempt 8: NEGATIVE — Detected failed client-journey checks: timing.</li></ol>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="records-heading">
      <h2 id="records-heading">Fixed fictional records</h2>
      <pre id="records" tabindex="0" aria-label="Inspectable fixed fictional records">{
  "boundary": "FIXED FICTIONAL TEACHING DATA ONLY — no operation was sent, authenticated, queued, fetched or saved.",
  "activeStage": "ready",
  "fixedOracle": {
    "banner": "Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result",
    "requestId": "request-fiction-140",
    "jobId": "job-fiction-140",
    "exportId": "export-fiction-140",
    "artifactId": "artifact-fiction-140",
    "owner": "identity-fiction-owner-140",
    "foreign": "identity-fiction-other-140",
    "bytes": [
      83,
      49,
      52,
      48,
      10,
      49,
      44,
      55,
      10
    ],
    "durations": {
      "submit": 5,
      "switchProcess": 1,
      "process": 12,
      "switchPoll": 1,
      "poll": 4,
      "switchDownload": 1,
      "download": 6,
      "check": 0,
      "reset": 0
    },
    "tiers": {
      "submit": "submit-v1",
      "process": "processor-v1",
      "poll": "poller-v1",
      "download": "download-v1"
    }
  },
  "activeJourney": null
}</pre>
